{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786993884,"nonce":"6YDmyQX5acGBh+5Yl61afmpASwg=","title":"`Leave` is implemented at three layers, emits an event, and is called from nowhere","message":"**What is wrong.** Group membership is never ended. `left_at` is always NULL, so every \"current\nmembers\" read returns everything that ever joined the generation — resolved and expired\noccurrences included.\n\n**The demonstration.** `Leave` exists at three layers:\n`internal/grouping/repository/member.go:117-122` (the `SET left_at = GREATEST(joined_at, $4)`\nupdate), `internal/grouping/service/service.go:391-410`, and the port at\n`internal/grouping/service/ports.go:51`. It emits `group.member_left` at `service.go:406`. A\nrepo-wide search for callers outside tests —\n`grep -rn \"Leave(\" internal/ --include=\"*.go\" | grep -v _test.go` — returns only those four\ndefinitions. Nothing calls it.\n\nFive things follow:\n\n1. Every current-membership read filters `WHERE left_at IS NULL` (`member.go:174, 268, 326,\n   404, 411, 490`), and that predicate now matches every row.\n2. `group.member_left` (`internal/alerts/domain/event.go:99`) is a declared, validated event\n   type that never appears on any timeline.\n3. `gm_current_idx` (migration 00044), partial on `left_at IS NULL`, narrows nothing.\n4. The point-in-time replay query — `joined_at \u003c= $3 AND (left_at IS NULL OR left_at \u003e $3)`,\n   `member.go:163-174` — can only ever show growth, so the promise at\n   `db/migrations/00008_grouping.sql:110-111` that the card \"can be replayed at any past\n   instant\" is monotonic by construction.\n5. Member rows are keyed `(group_id, occurrence_id)`, so an alert that resolves and re-fires\n   outside the grace window within one generation gets a *second* row, also `left_at IS NULL` —\n   the same alert listed twice, once resolved and once firing. With `group_close_delay` and\n   `refire_grace` both at 1200s (`platform/tuning/defaults.go:74, 96`) that is easily reachable.\n\nIt went unnoticed because group close runs off `last_activity_at`, a timestamp, not off\nmembership — so the missing call has never broken closing.\n\n**Why it matters.** The group card is the signature UI view (`ev_group_idx` \"serves §D.12(b),\nthe GROUP TIMELINE\"). It currently answers \"everything that was ever wrong in this generation\"\nwhile appearing to answer \"what is wrong now\". An overstated count and a list padded with\nresolved members are the two ways an operator loses the ability to read the shape of an\nincident off the card.\n\nThe resolution is not to wire the call up. Once the group key is derived from the case's own\nlabels, membership is a *function of the case* rather than a recorded event: Case → Group\nbecomes many-to-one (multi-membership disappears with `receiver` leaving the key), and\n`alert_cases.group_id` — already present at `db/migrations/00007_alerts.sql:123`, its FK added\nin 00008, indexed by `occ_group_idx` at `:191` — is sufficient. `member_joined` and\n`member_left` were facts about the **case**, phrased as if the group were the actor.\n\n**Where.** `internal/grouping/repository/member.go:29, 56, 117-122, 163-180, 268, 326, 334,\n398-411, 490`; `internal/grouping/service/service.go:391-410`;\n`internal/grouping/service/ports.go:51`; `internal/alerts/domain/event.go:93-103`;\n`db/migrations/00008_grouping.sql:92-114`;\n`db/migrations/00044_group_member_preview_index.sql`.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.** `alert_group_members` is gone, membership is read from `alert_cases.group_id`,\nand `Leave` no longer exists at any layer. `group.member_joined` and `group.member_left` are\nremoved from the event vocabulary and from the migration comments that describe them.\n`group.opened`, `group.closed`, `group.storm_started` and `group.storm_ended` survive — those\nare genuinely facts about the group. The `gm_*` indexes and the preview index are dropped.\n\nGroup close changes with it: close on **\"no live case with this split key\"** rather than on\n`last_activity_at`, so a generation cannot close over a case that is still open. Storm counting\nis unaffected — `EvaluateStorm` counts joins in a window, and joins still happen.\n\nA test asserts that a group's member list contains only cases that are currently open, and that\nan alert which resolved and re-fired within one generation appears once.\n\n**Depends on** the derived group key ticket. The deletion is only correct once membership is\ncomputable.","files":null}]}